    <miscellaneous>
      <miscellaneous-field name="analysis-json">{"meta":{"id":"schumann_op15_7_traumerei","parent_item_id":"schumann_op15_7_traumerei","title":"Träumerei","composer":"Robert Schumann","source_file":"files/scores/schumann_op15_7_traumerei.mid","quarter_range":[0,97.0],"bar_quarters":4.0,"pickup_quarters":1.0,"time_signature":"4/4","key":"F","tempo":60.0,"midi_play_url":"files/scores/schumann_op15_7_traumerei.mid","source_licence":"PD","source_page":"https://www.mutopiaproject.org/cgibin/piece-info.cgi?id=504","quantisation_divisors":[4,8],"notation_notes":"Mutopia MIDI (PD edition): one-quarter C4 pickup at quarter 0, bar 1 at quarter 1, 24 bars of 4/4 to quarter 97. No triplets; straight grid. The printed repeats (bars 1–8 and 9–24) are not unfolded in the MIDI and are not added. Spread bass grace notes (Bb2 bar 2/18, C#3 bar 6) sound 0.125 q before beat 2. MIDI-derived score, not an Urtext; bar 22 fermata appears only as a tempo drop.","suggested_arrangement_tempo":100,"sustain_events":[]},"draft":false,"reviewed_by":"claude-opus-5-5 (MusicBot) 2026-10-11","summary":"An F-major rising theme in regular four-bar phrases. A (bars 1–8) ends with a half cadence, then cadences in C. B (9–16) restates the opening and sequences it into G minor and then D minor (tonicized, not established keys) before a Bbmaj7 turns back to a half cadence in F. A′ (17–24) repeats bars 1–4 and closes with a G9 peak and a perfect cadence.","sections":[{"name":"Pickup","start_bar":0,"end_bar":0,"mood":["hushed"],"description":"Lone C4 upbeat."},{"name":"A","start_bar":1,"end_bar":8,"mood":["tender","nostalgic"],"description":"4+4: I–IV rise, HC bar 4; second phrase via A7/C# and Fm to a PAC in tonicized C."},{"name":"B (sequence)","start_bar":9,"end_bar":16,"mood":["yearning","wistful"],"description":"Bars 9–12 tonicize G minor; 13–16 repeat it a fourth higher in D minor; Bbmaj7 → HC in F."},{"name":"A′","start_bar":17,"end_bar":24,"mood":["warm","settling"],"description":"Bars 17–20 = 1–4; G9 peak in bar 22; PAC in bar 24."}],"tricks":["Bars 1–2: rising melody to a held top note over I–IV, with the accompaniment entering off the beat.","Bars 3 and 19: V7 → V9 as the melody steps down, then a passing I6 before the half cadence.","Bars 10 and 14: a suspended minor ninth (Eb5 over D, Bb5 over A) that resolves down by step.","Bars 9–16: the same four-bar model up a fourth, G minor then D minor, without changing key.","Bar 16: Dm/A → Bbmaj7 → C swerves away from D minor back to F.","Bar 22: applied G9 with the melody on its ninth, then the cadence is delayed through ii6 and V/ii."],"loop_candidates":[{"start_bar":1,"end_bar":4,"why":"I–IV–V7–I6–V–I–V ends on a half cadence that leads back into bar 1; needs the C pickup on the seam.","quarter_range":[1,17],"requires_audition":true},{"start_bar":9,"end_bar":16,"why":"Sequence ends on V of F, which resolves to bar 9 F.","quarter_range":[33,65],"requires_audition":true}],"hook_candidates":[{"start_bar":0,"end_bar":2,"why":"C–F leap and climb to the held F5 over IV: the famous opening.","quarter_range":[0,9]},{"start_bar":21,"end_bar":24,"why":"G9 climax and the closing cadence."}],"kpop_uses":[{"where":"verse","why":"Bars 1–4 (pickup included) as a soft piano bed; four-bar phrases fit a vocal line."},{"where":"pre-chorus","why":"Bars 13–16: rising sequence into D minor, ending on V of F to set up a chorus."},{"where":"bridge","why":"Bars 9–12 move into G minor for a darker contrast with the same melody."},{"where":"chorus","why":"Bars 21–24 (G9 peak, delayed cadence, PAC) as an emotional closing hook; no key change exists in the source."}],"review_flags":[{"bar":0,"reason":"Pickup confirmed from the LilyPond \\partial 4 and the MIDI onset; the draft omitted it, so all its bar labels were one beat early."},{"bar":8,"reason":"Beat-3 C arrival has no G in the MIDI (root+third only); the label is retained and fails the mechanical check."},{"bar":8,"reason":"Cadence in C is read as a tonicized dominant inside F; a short modulation to V is also a defensible reading."},{"bar":9,"reason":"Draft F→D minor and D minor→F modulations removed: G minor (bars 10–12) and D minor (14–16) are tonicizations; no structural cadence in either."},{"bar":12,"reason":"G-minor dominant on beat 2.5 has no F#, and beat 4 has only G2–A2 under F4; both left as ? rather than forced."},{"bar":16,"reason":"Dm/A on beat 3 could be heard as an unresolved 6/4 rather than a tonic arrival; labelled vi64 either way."},{"bar":22,"reason":"Bar 22 tempo drop interpreted as the editions' fermata; dynamics are not inferred."}],"mood":[{"start_bar":0,"end_bar":0,"labels":["hushed"]},{"start_bar":1,"end_bar":8,"labels":["tender","nostalgic"]},{"start_bar":9,"end_bar":16,"labels":["yearning","wistful"]},{"start_bar":17,"end_bar":24,"labels":["warm","settling"]}],"schema_version":1,"bars":[{"bar":0,"start_quarter":0,"duration_quarters":1.0,"key":"F","chords":[{"beat":1.0,"symbol":"?","rn":"?","function":"dominant pickup","reason":"Lone C4 pickup; no third or fifth sounds."}],"events":[{"type":"story","technique":"start","text":"start: a single C rising into the tonic, the dream opens"},{"type":"hook","technique":"melodic_cell","text":"Pickup C4 leaps up a fourth to F4, then climbs F–A–C–F to a held F5 over IV"}]},{"bar":1,"start_quarter":1.0,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"F","chords":[{"beat":1.0,"symbol":"F","rn":"I","function":"tonic"}],"events":[{"type":"form","technique":"theme_1","text":"A: four-bar phrase rising through the F chord"},{"type":"rhythm_phrase","technique":"phrase_length","text":"Regular 4+4 bar phrases throughout (bars 1–4, 5–8, 9–12, 13–16, 17–20, 21–24)"},{"type":"voicing_orchestration","technique":"open_spacing","text":"Low F2 bass with inner C3–F3–A3–C4 entering on beat 2 under the held melody F4","beat":2.0},{"type":"rhythm_phrase","technique":"syncopation","text":"Accompaniment enters on beat 2, after the melody and bass","beat":2.0}]},{"bar":2,"start_quarter":5.0,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":